course: dictionary
lesson: 12047
title: Circumstances: the conditions around an event
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Circumstances is a noun, and it is nearly always used in the plural. It means the facts or conditions that surround a situation and affect what happens. «The circumstances of the accident were reported on the news.» The word tells you that the reasons and conditions behind the accident matter, not just the accident itself.
explain: Some phrases with circumstances are very common. «Under no circumstances» means never, or not at all. «Under no circumstances should you touch a broken wire» is a safety rule: the answer is always no. Notice how strong the words are.
explain: «In the circumstances» means because of what has happened. «In the circumstances, the teacher let us go home early» means the teacher made that choice because of something that had happened, such as a storm or an emergency. The word can also mean money and living conditions. «The family lived in difficult circumstances after the flood» means they had little money and a hard life.
fact: Circumstances is a noun, and it is usually plural.
fact: «Under no circumstances» means never, not at all.
fact: «In the circumstances» means because of what has happened.
fact: «Difficult circumstances» can mean that a person has little money or hard living conditions.
fact: Formal writing and news reports often use circumstances, so look for the clues around it to understand what it means.
exercise: «Under no circumstances should you touch a broken wire.» What does «under no circumstances» mean? | *Never, not at all | Only on a sunny day | Sometimes, if you are careful | Quickly and quietly
exercise: «In the circumstances, the teacher let us go home early.» What does «in the circumstances» mean? | Very slowly | *Because of what has happened | Before lunch | Without any reason at all
exercise: The news report explained the circumstances of the storm. What are circumstances? | *The facts or conditions that affect a situation | A sudden loud noise | A type of cloud | A kind of bus ticket
test: «The family lived in difficult circumstances after the flood.» What does circumstances mean here? | Songs they sang together | Rules about school | Shops and markets | *Money and living conditions
test: «Under no circumstances should you open the door to a stranger.» What does this sentence tell you? | Open it only at night | Open the door quickly | *Never open the door to a stranger | Always open it when it rains
exam: «The match was cancelled, and in these circumstances nobody could play safely.» What does «in these circumstances» mean? | Under a big tree | *Because of what has happened | Happily, with a cheer | Before the match started
